  "body": "Process change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\n## What changed\n- A `needs-rework` finding does not turn a ready PR back into a draft. The author pushes the fix to the same PR. A push moves the head, so the earlier review and `merge-ready` do not count for the new head.\n- An orange `conflicts` verdict still makes one of our own PRs a draft.\n- The first `needs-rework` comment names the class of each finding and asks for one rule that closes the class.\n- Files: `AGENTS.md` (three passages), `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`, `.claude/skills/resolve-conflicts/SKILL.md`, and the decision file `docs/decisions/3727-ready-flag-stays.md`.\n\n## Why\nData from 2026-11-20 to 2026-11-23: 30 PRs, 36 switches from ready to draft. 27 followed `needs-rework`, 3 followed `conflicts`, 6 had no label cause. The median time from ready to draft is 1.6 hours. #3283 and #3284 flipped three times each. Each round trip costs one more read and one more trial.\n\n## Authority\nThe maintainer ordered this change on 2026-11-23: \"Do your changes as a docs changes, push it and merge it and announce it one go.. On my call.\" The independent review is waived by that order.\n\n## Not exercised\nNo code, no label and no workflow changes. The PROCESS_VERSION bump follows after the merge, as AGENTS.md says.\n\nFixes #3727\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
